  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council; \"the elections take place on January 15th\". Nominations were received in the Tontine on Monday 6 January (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1908, p. 5). Each party nominated only for the ward it held, and \"in Armagh all the candidates nominated have been returned unopposed, which leaves the representation unchanged\". The Unionists handed in no papers for this ward (the North Ward of 1905 and 1911)."
